# Empire of Minds — tooling credentials (template).
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values locally. `.env` is git-ignored and must
# never be committed. These variables are read ONLY by backend/tooling under
# `tools/`; the Godot gameplay client never sees a provider credential.
#
# Nothing in this file may contain a real secret. Values here are descriptions.

# Asset generation provider: images and image-to-3D meshes.
# Used by: python -m tools.assetgen (meshy adapter)
MESHY_API_KEY=

# Character auto-rig provider.
# Used by: python -m tools.assetgen autorig (uthana adapter)
UTHANA_API_KEY=

# Optional endpoint overrides, normally left unset.
#
# These are part of the APPROVAL, not just configuration. The canonical endpoint
# identity - scheme, normalised host, port and base path - is inside the provider
# plan's SHA-256, so changing one of these invalidates every digest generated
# against the previous value, and a submission whose current endpoint disagrees
# with the approved plan is refused before the credential is read. That is
# deliberate: a credential must never travel to a host nobody approved.
#
# https is mandatory for live traffic; an http endpoint cannot be authorized at
# all. A fake endpoint for tests belongs in test-owned configuration, never here.
# MESHY_API_BASE=https://api.meshy.ai
# UTHANA_API_BASE=https://api.uthana.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Proxies are NOT inherited, deliberately.
#
# `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY` and `ALL_PROXY` are ignored for provider traffic:
# the transport builds its opener with proxies explicitly disabled. A proxy is a
# redirection of authenticated traffic, and a loopback proxy is exactly the case
# the offline network tripwire permits, so inheriting one silently would move a
# credential somewhere unapproved without tripping anything. If a proxy is ever
# genuinely needed it must be an explicitly supported, approval-bound setting -
# not an ambient variable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paid-call opt-in. NOT a credential.
#
# This is barrier 2 of the three required for any live provider call. It says
# "this MACHINE may spend money", which is a different statement from "this
# command intends to reach a provider" (the --live flag) and from "this exact
# plan was read and approved" (--confirm-plan <sha256> from `provider-plan`).
#
# Leave it UNSET. Having credentials configured is not permission, and neither
# is --live on its own. Only the exact value 1 counts; 0, false, yes and true
# are all refusals. The test suite clears this variable, so a suite can never
# inherit an opt-in left over from a real run.
# EOM_ALLOW_PAID_PROVIDER_CALLS=1
